\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{3}{Four verification layers organized into two stages for the specified VQE instance. Logical, numeric, and probabilistic verification produce results before execution using their own formalisms. Runtime verification checks logical and numeric obligations for individual runs and compares probabilistic predictions with repeated executions. The verification record associates these checks with the same configuration and source files. The displayed verdict names match the implementation. Probabilistic verdicts are interpreted under the stated assumptions and statistical decision rule}{figure.1}{}}
