\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Cumulative probability of first satisfying $E_{\rm  ideal}(z)-E_{\rm  ref}\leq 0.02\xspace  $ versus optimizer iteration. The solid staircase is Gaussian-DTMC forward propagation, circles are Storm checkpoints, and the dashed staircase summarizes 400\xspace  independently seeded ideal-Born finite-shot runs with 1,024\xspace  shots per group/candidate. The shaded region gives pointwise 95\% Wilson intervals at each iteration. It is not a simultaneous confidence band. Both processes use the same success predicate, candidate rule, and resource configuration.}}{8}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:probability-comparison}{{4}{8}{Cumulative probability of first satisfying $E_{\rm ideal}(z)-E_{\rm ref}\leq \GapThreshold $ versus optimizer iteration. The solid staircase is Gaussian-DTMC forward propagation, circles are Storm checkpoints, and the dashed staircase summarizes \BaselineRuns independently seeded ideal-Born finite-shot runs with \ShotsPerGroup shots per group/candidate. The shaded region gives pointwise 95\% Wilson intervals at each iteration. It is not a simultaneous confidence band. Both processes use the same success predicate, candidate rule, and resource configuration}{figure.4}{}}
